.SH NAME
niac-list - List interfaces and demo content


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBniac list [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
List the same operator-facing resources the legacy Java demo
wrapper exposed: network interfaces, runnable scenarios, SNMP walks, and
packet captures.

.PP
Scenario output includes built-in templates and installed library networks.
Walk and capture output reads the on-disk content library.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for list

.PP
\fB--root\fP=""
	Library root (default: NIAC_LIBRARY_ROOT or ~/.niac/library)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--storage-keep\fP=500
	Run history records to keep, pruned oldest first on start (0 keeps every run)

.PP
\fB--storage-path\fP=""
	Path to NIAC run history database (default: ~/.niac/niac.db)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  # List usable network interfaces
  niac list interfaces

  # List runnable scenarios
  niac list scenarios

  # List SNMP walks, optionally scoped by vendor/path prefix
  niac list walks
  niac list walks cisco

  # List packet captures
  niac list captures
.EE


